BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:crh-20260612-kimmins
DTSTART:20260612T140000
DTEND:20260612T150000
SUMMARY:CRH Seminar: FROM INHERITANCE TO INTERVENTION - Reprogramming the Sperm Epigenome
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Professor Sarah Kimmins (University of Montreal)\nHost: Niamh Forde\n\nSenior Tier 1 Canada Research Chair in Epigenetic Inheritance of Disease. Research on how paternal environment shapes sperm epigenetic programming. Also Founder and CEO of HisTurn (male fertility diagnostics).
LOCATION:IRR SOUTH, SEMINAR ROOM (1.05)
ORGANIZER;CN=CRH Seminars:mailto:crh.seminars@ed.ac.uk
END:VEVENT
