BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cvs-20260610-lygate
DTSTART:20260610T120000
DTEND:20260610T130000
SUMMARY:SEMINAR SERIES: A tale of two metabolites - Creatine and Homoarginine in Heart Disease
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Craig Lygate (University of Glasgow)\nHost: Cecile Benezech\n\nTitle: "A tale of two metabolites: the therapeutic potential of creatine and homoarginine in heart disease"\n\nCreatine matches energy supply and demand in the heart. Homoarginine associated with poor outcomes in CVD.\n\nPizza social 13:00-13:30 at The Larder.\n\n⚠️ Pizza provided after at The Larder
LOCATION:Auditorium A, Shirley Hall, Chancellors Building
ORGANIZER;CN=Rosie Adam:mailto:rosie.adam@ed.ac.uk
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ebr-20260601-hore
DTSTART:20260601T133000
DTEND:20260601T143000
SUMMARY:EBR Seminar: Unlocking the Female Ribosome and the Epigenetic Androgen Clock
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Professor Tim Hore (University of Otago, New Zealand)\nHost: Dr Doug Vernimmen\n\nPart 1: fem-rDNA knockout in zebrafish - effectively blocked female differentiation.\nPart 2: Androgen Clock - predictor of long-term male hormone exposure from DNA methylation.
LOCATION:Roslin Institute Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN=Douglas Vernimmen:mailto:douglas.vernimmen@roslin.ed.ac.uk
END:VEVENT
